Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] pinctrl: qcom: match A16 Windows DMIC pin settings

The installed Windows calibration selects GPIO6/7 with pull-downs and slew
code 1. Its raw drive value 3 is scaled and quantized by the shipped DSP to
the 4 mA hardware setting. The GPIO setter places slew in CFG bits 12:11.

Use separate Glymur group data to enable slew on these two pins without
changing SM8650 groups. Apply drive 4 mA, pull-downs and slew 1 on the A16.
The previous 2 mA experiment worsened camera bands; it is not included here.

Built and installed for testing, but cold-boot and camera/microphone validation
remain pending. This is a reversible experiment, not a confirmed banding fix.
No Windows driver or firmware bytes are included.

